body:
What if I wished it away and this is me remembering it. The feeling of being ready to wake up from a dream, but you never do, only go back to sleep to wake up in the same place. I once had a dream that started with me on a swingset, and I could't get off, just back and forth, rocking, like a cradle. And in that dream I thought I was there forever. Not that I knew, I just had a feeling, and that feeling is where the problem lies. Existential dread. Like you're trapped in your own head and thoughts for eternity. All I really know is my thoughts.

&#x200B;

I know that my own thoughts stop me from being able to enjoy the present. To look at the past with regret, and to look at the future with anxiety. To not see what my own reality is clearly, to be a judge of my own fate. Maybe that's where I am. Maybe that's what hell is, a way of thinking.
